== (3) Collatz on Q_odd: periodicity in a box, cycles per denominator, the sheet symmetry ==
 odd-numerator rationals m/d, |m| <= 40, d <= 40 odd: 634 points; not eventually periodic within 600 steps or before 10^15: 0 []
 distinct cycles reached, by denominator (d: least elements): {1: ['-1', '-7', '-91', '1'], 5: ['1/5', '19/5', '23/5'], 7: ['5/7'], 11: ['-29/11', '1/11', '13/11'], 13: ['1/13', '131/13'], 17: ['-179/17', '1/17', '23/17'], 19: ['5/19'], 23: ['41/23', '5/23', '7/23'], 25: ['17/25', '7/25'], 29: ['1/29', '11/29'], 31: ['13/31'], 35: ['13/35', '17/35']}
 cycles with 3 | denominator: [] (clocks are coprime to 3, so none: preperiodic points may have 3 | d, cycle points cannot)
 sheet symmetry: the fixed point of a word for 3x-1 is minus the fixed point for 3x+1: True (negation conjugates the two sheets on Z_(2))
