== (5) the Eckmann-Hilton defect ==
 multipliers commute: 3 * (1/2) = (1/2) * 3; affine letters do not: the words (1,2) and (2,1) have carries 5, 7, defect beta = -2, so the two composites differ by the translation -1/4
 the multiplier monoid <2, 3> is N x N (two commuting copies of N); the carry cocycle is the obstruction to interchange, and it is antisymmetric (twelfth note): the structure is symmetric, which is exactly what Eckmann-Hilton would force if the interchange held
